{"name":"Aqua Whisper","hex":"#bfdfdf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"},{"term":"whisper","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of speaking in a quiet voice, especially without vibration of the vocal cords; the sound thus produced.","A rumor."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter words without sonant breath; to talk without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound.","To say (something) softly or under one's breath, so as to be heard only by one near at hand; to utter (something) without sonant breath, without that vibration of the vocal cords which gives sonorous, or vocal, sound."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whisper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t